        "original_id": "a35e7eaf-8f0c-5317-b08d-a11fffde1b1a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hidesaburō Ueno\n- Animals: Hachikō\n- Places: Japan, Ōdate, Akita Prefecture\n- Roles: agricultural scientist, guardian, owner\n\nFacts:\n- Hidesaburō Ueno was born on January 19, 1872, and died on May 21, 1925.\n- Hidesaburō Ueno, sometimes written as Ueno Hidesamurō, was a Japanese agricultural scientist.\n- Hidesaburō Ueno was famous in Japan as the guardian of Hachikō.\n- Hachikō was born on November 10, 1923, on a farm near Ōdate in Akita Prefecture, Japan.\n- Hachikō was an Akita dog.\n- After Hidesaburō Ueno died, Hachikō continued to wait for his owner for more than nine years.\n- Hachikō died on March 8, 1935, and is remembered for his remarkable loyalty to Hidesaburō Ueno.",
